<title>OMAN: Oil pushes Oman's trade surplus up in July.</title>
<headline>Oil pushes Oman's trade surplus up in July.</headline>
<dateline>MUSCAT 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oman's trade surplus rose to 100.5 million rials in July from 78.4 million in June, latest Ministry of Development figures show.</p>
<p>		    July '96   June '96   May '96   1995</p>
<p> Total exports   244.8	214.1	214.7     2,333.2</p>
<p> Oil		 196.2	165.4	170.0     1,829.3</p>
<p> Non-oil	    11.7	 15.4	 15.2	 182.0</p>
<p> Re-exports	 36.9	 33.3	 29.5	 321.9</p>
<p> Imports	   144.3	135.7	153.6     1,633.6</p>
<p> Trade balance  +100.5	+78.4	+61.1	+699.6</p>
<p>Note: Figures are in millions of rials. Slight discrepancies in figures are due to rounding.</p>
</text>
